      "conditions": "Wide scanf %s or %[ without l converts into a narrow destination and adds a second null byte after the shift-state terminator. Exact destination exhaustion can cause a one-byte null overwrite. Narrow scanf, wide-output l conversions and allocating a/m conversions are outside this defect."
