      "observed_debian_sid_status": "2.43-7 vulnerable; unstable unfixed",
      "conditions": "Allocation failure during POSIX regex compilation or matching can leave stale realloc pointers in re_dfa_add_node, build_range_exp or match_ctx_add_entry; subsequent cleanup can free them again. This is not limited to deliberately crafted patterns; memory pressure is a condition, not a general mitigation."
